. "$GRIMOIRE"/CMAKE_FUNCTIONS
           SPELL=dspfilters
         VERSION=1.10.0
          SOURCE=iir1-$VERSION.tar.gz
SOURCE_DIRECTORY=$BUILD_DIRECTORY/iir1-$VERSION
        WEB_SITE=https://github.com/berndporr/iir1
   SOURCE_URL[0]=$WEB_SITE/archive/refs/tags/$VERSION.tar.gz
     SOURCE_HASH=sha512:f50b925394f79662ae021c02e60667273a5d4615f2ef9f88d256c3c6dbb0f7d851207b65e2da56b69a97e576b3bb611653fde421df4ae0a952615d29be2f33a6
      LICENSE[0]=MIT
         ENTERED=20260927
           SHORT="IIR filter library for audio processing"
cat << EOF
A library implementing infinite impulse response filters with a C++ API
similar to the Berkeley DSPFilters library. It provides the building blocks
to design and cascade Butterworth, Chebyshev, elliptic and biquad filters,
and it is used by DOSBox Staging to shape and resample its audio output.

The library installs as libiir, with a pkg-config file (iir) and a CMake
package (iir) exporting the iir::iir and iir::iir_static targets.
